3D Printing Settings Prompt (Optimized for ABS)

    Material: ABS (Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene)
    Printer Model: Prusa CoreOne (or equivalent)

    Core Parameters:

        Layer Height: 0.2mm (Standard for balance between speed and strength).

        Infill Density: 20% - 25% (To support the weight of 11.1V batteries and motors).

        Infill Pattern: Gyroid or Grid (For multi-directional structural strength).

        Nozzle Temperature: 260°C.

        Bed Temperature: 110°C.

    Critical Structural Settings:

        Supports: Enable "Support on build plate only". Use Organic or Snug style to ensure the motor housing and ESP32 slot ceilings don't sag.

        Brim: Enable Brim with a width of 5mm to 8mm. This is essential to prevent corner warping/lifting, which is common with ABS.

        Cooling: Keep the fan speed at a minimum (10-20%) or OFF for the first few layers to prevent cracking/delamination.

        Perimeters (Walls): Set to at least 3 wall loops for a tough, durable chassis